Add public flushInMemoryCache() method to Registry.

Registry (SingletonInterface) caches `sys_registry` database rows in
the `$entries` array, with `$loadedNamespaces` tracking which
namespaces have been hydrated from DB. Under PHP-FPM the cache dies
with the process, so an out-of-band write to sys_registry (scheduler
task, other worker, install-tool maintenance action) is visible on
the next request. Under long-running runtimes the cache persists,
so subsequent requests keep returning pre-write values for feature
flags, install-tool locks, schema versions, etc.

Add a public `flushInMemoryCache()` method so the in-memory cache
can be cleared without reaching into protected properties. The next
`get()` call will reload the namespace from the database.

diff --git a/Classes/Registry.php b/Classes/Registry.php
--- a/Classes/Registry.php
+++ b/Classes/Registry.php
@@ -187,4 +187,17 @@
             throw new \InvalidArgumentException('Given namespace must be longer than two characters.', 1249755131);
         }
     }
+
+    /**
+     * Flushes the in-memory cache of registry entries.
+     *
+     * The next get() call will reload the namespace from the database.
+     * Useful for long-running PHP runtimes where the singleton instance
+     * persists across requests and cached values may become stale.
+     */
+    public function flushInMemoryCache(): void
+    {
+        $this->entries = [];
+        $this->loadedNamespaces = [];
+    }
 }
